# Development Workflow (Project Default)

## Plan and verify before coding

- Reuse existing patterns in the repo before adding new abstractions.
- Keep changes scoped: one task, one coherent diff.
- For non-trivial changes, define a short checklist: implementation, validation, docs.

## Safety and change discipline

- Never break existing user flows: landing, auth, booking, dashboard.
- Prefer incremental refactors over broad rewrites.
- Do not introduce silent fallbacks that hide errors.

## Definition of done

- Run relevant checks (`lint`, build/type checks if touched areas are sensitive).
- Update docs when behavior, setup, or env requirements change.
- Include clear error handling and user-facing messages for failure states.
